  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "t:names.image_with_text",
      "category": "t:categories.storytelling",
      "blocks": {
        "eyebrow_1": {
          "type": "_section-eyebrow",
          "settings": {
            "text": "Founded 2021"
          }
        },
        "heading_2": {
          "type": "_section-heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Fragrance as a daily ritual, not a finishing touch",
            "size": "h2",
            "tag": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_3": {
          "type": "_section-text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>We started in a small studio with a perfumer, a botanist and a wall of mood boards. Every scent is built backwards: first the feeling, then the plants traditionally linked to it, then the composition.</p><p>The result is a collection of six genderless eau de parfums, body veils and home scents designed to be worn on purpose.</p>",
            "size": "large"
          }
        },
        "button_4": {
          "type": "_section-button",
          "settings": {
            "label": "Explore the collection",
            "link": "",
            "style": "dark"
          }
        }
      },
